+// One complete, coherent battery status.
+//
+// Delegates to base::xrio::ParseBatteryStatus rather than restating the rules,
+// and that is the point of the split: a launch-time validator and a call-site
+// read that each carry their own copy of "what is coherent" is how a tuple gets
+// refused by one and honoured by the other. The accessor fails closed on
+// exactly what this refuses, so the two answers cannot diverge.
+bool BatteryStatusTuple(std::string_view value, std::string* error) {
+  BatteryStatus ignored;
+  return ParseBatteryStatus(value, &ignored, error);
+}
