+  // different reason than when this test was first written.
+  //
+  // v4 was pinned to 151.0.7922.108, a Chromium tag BETWEEN Chrome releases, so
+  // "the build's own version" was a string no real client has ever sent. The
+  // reduced navigator.userAgent hid that; the four high-entropy UA-CH surfaces
+  // did not. The fork is pinned to 151.0.7922.137 now, a real Linux stable, so
+  // reporting the build is reporting a released Chrome.
+  //
+  // What makes that safe is not this default, it is the gate behind it:
+  // tools/check_ua_version.py refuses a CHROMIUM_VERSION that is not on
+  // fork/released-chrome-versions.txt while this knob is absent. Re-pin onto a
